From 8cf7b140ca5fbba567d5dff06aa2f3c43aaea057 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Duprey <509630+destinal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:08:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/17] Claude Code plugin: sessions panel, tab dots,
 notifications

- The Claude Sessions panel lists every session that shows a status, in
  every Konsole window: a dot, the tab title and the status in its color,
  then the detail. Sessions needing the user come first (waiting, error,
  done, working, idle), the most recent first among equals. Clicking one
  brings it forward. The panel starts hidden; the window remembers it.
- Each session's tab shows its status dot.
- A session the user is not looking at notifies when it starts waiting
  (ClaudeCodeWaiting) or finishes or fails (ClaudeCodeFinished), with an
  action that brings it forward, at most once per event every 10 seconds.
  Both events are configurable in Konsole's notification settings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
